Hello Phil

I am trying to fit a bifactor model with only one specific factor. There are 12 items in the test. Seven items (in random order) load on a specific factor but the other 5 items don’t load on any specific factor and load only on the general factor. How should I specify this in ‘mirt’?

If there were two specific factors, that would have been easy like below. But with only one specific factor I don't know what to do. What should I insert for the items that only belong to the general factor?

 specific <- c(1,1,2,1,1,1,2,1,2,1,2,2)

 Thanks for your help.

Afshin

--

